; Regression test for issue #3327: a stock split is not an unrealized
; gain or loss, but a later price change is.
;
; The split's own prices put AAPL at $5 on the day of the split, which
; values the 10 shares held before it at $50.  That $450 drop is offset
; by the split itself, which exchanges those shares at their $500 cost
; basis (#1821).  The rise from $5 to $6 that follows is a gain of $100
; on the 100 shares, and is booked even though the next transaction is
; on a later date.

2024-01-01 Opening balance
    Assets:Vault     10 XYZ {$10.00}
    Equity:Opening

2024-01-01 Buy
    Assets:Broker    10 AAPL @ $50
    Assets:Cash

2024-01-02 Stock split
    Assets:Broker   -10 AAPL @ $50
    Assets:Broker   100 AAPL @ $5

P 2024-02-01 AAPL $6

2024-03-01 Interest
    Assets:Cash       $10
    Income:Interest

test bal -V --unrealized --now 2024/06/01
                $110
              10 XYZ  Assets
                $600    Broker
               $-490    Cash
              10 XYZ    Vault
               $-100
             -10 XYZ  Equity
             -10 XYZ    Opening
               $-100    Unrealized Gains
                $-10  Income:Interest
--------------------
                   0
end test

; XYZ has no price, so the report cannot value it: it carries no gain or
; loss, whatever its lot price.
test bal -V --unrealized --now 2024/06/01 Vault
              10 XYZ  Assets:Vault
end test

; --gain pairs each total's market value with its cost, which leaves no
; basis to compare, so it books only the revaluation since the last
; posting, the rise from $5 to $6, and never the fall at the split.
test bal -G --unrealized --now 2024/06/01 Broker
                $100  Assets:Broker
               $-100  Equity:Unrealized Gains
--------------------
                   0
end test

; cleared keeps two totals for each account, which leave no basis to compare,
; so it too books only the revaluation since the last posting.
test cleared -V --unrealized --now 2024/06/01 Broker
            $600                   0                 Assets:Broker
           $-100                                     Equity:Unrealized Gains
----------------  ------------------    ---------
            $500                   0             
end test
